COMMERCIAL S11.2-R15 EPOCH HISTORY PRIVILEGE DIAGNOSIS

Date: 2026-09-23
Status: ROOT_CAUSE_CONFIRMED; AUTOMATIC_ROLLBACK_GREEN; R15_1_FIX_AUTHORIZED

Observed deployment result

- The exact r2 freeze passed the canonical preflight.
- A root-owned, mode-0700 predeploy backup was created and verified at
  `/opt/tu1nz_repos/backups/commercial-s11-2-canary-bootstrap/20260923T185303Z-predeploy`.
- Application and Control switched to the exact r2-bound target commits.
- Migration 0034 committed successfully and created the append-only terminal
  epoch history table and the privileged rearm function.
- The controller then stopped before rearming the terminal epoch because its
  runtime-DSN read of `commercial_s11_canary_epoch_history` returned PostgreSQL
  `INSUFFICIENT_PRIVILEGE`.
- The versioned rollback restored both source commits, packages and bounded
  runtime artifacts.  Both repositories are clean at their source commits;
  S7, S8 Landing, S8 Telegram, S10 WMS and nginx are active with zero restarts;
  all public WMS endpoints are GREEN; the S11 controller is not installed.

Root cause

Migration 0034 intentionally leaves the append-only terminal epoch history
table private to the database administrator.  The controller nevertheless
uses `database_scalar`, which connects through the least-privilege runtime DSN,
to count history rows before and after the administrator-only rearm call.  The
write path correctly uses local `runuser -u postgres -- psql`; the verification
read path uses the wrong database ingress.

Classification

CONTROL_ADMIN_READ_INGRESS_MISMATCH

Bounded correction

- Do not grant the runtime role access to the administrator-only history table.
- Add a narrow controller helper that performs only scalar administrator reads
  through local `runuser -u postgres -- psql`.
- Use that helper only for the two epoch-history count reads around the rearm.
- Keep all ordinary runtime state and health reads on the least-privilege DSN.
- Add tests proving the runtime DSN is not used for epoch-history reads and the
  administrator helper cannot accept multi-statement or unbound input.
- Rebind the controller hashes and immutable r3 freeze only after full tests,
  review, merge-commit and post-merge CI are GREEN.

Backup and retry contract

- Keep the verified r2 predeploy backup immutable; do not reuse it for retry.
- A retry requires a new timestamped root-owned mode-0700 backup.
- Do not move the r2 tag.  Publish a new exact annotated freeze.
- Run exactly one backup-first retry after the R15.1 source release is GREEN.
- The existing automatic rollback remains authoritative for any retry failure.

Unchanged boundaries

- Maximum ten REAL SFW Canary sessions and a 24-hour bounded epoch.
- At least five valid REAL samples plus GREEN technical SLO before promotion.
- UNKNOWN provenance fails closed; human acceptance remains DEFERRED.
- Adult media, AVS, payment, external publishing, controlled beta and
  production remain CLOSED.

R15.2 bounded correction

- The r3 retry proved that the administrator-only history readback, terminal
  epoch rearm, feature-OFF health, synthetic journey, technical latency, hard
  gates and Canary activation all work through `S11_2_CANARY_RUNTIME_GREEN`.
- Final evidence collation then treated the optional
  `synthetic-journeys.json.*` companions as mandatory.  With no match, Bash
  passed the literal glob to `mv` and triggered the fail-closed rollback.
- Keep the primary synthetic journey JSON mandatory.  Move zero, one or many
  real companion files with an explicit bounded loop, while preserving fatal
  handling for an existing non-file or a real move error.
- Prove the shell contract with isolated zero-, one- and three-companion
  fixtures plus a non-file rejection fixture.
- Keep the r2 and r3 freezes and their verified backups immutable.  The first
  r4 tag was rejected before server mutation because two provenance literals
  did not match the controller's exact contract; it also remains immutable.
  The corrected deployable target is r5 and requires a fresh verified backup.
